  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The provision of Clean Energy Innovation Facility (CEIF) platform monitoring evaluation and learning (MEL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The umbrella Clean Energy Innovation Facility (CEIF) platform is one of the key platforms contributing to delivering the UK Government&#x2019;s &#xa3;1bn Ayrton Fund ICF commitment for clean energy in developing countries. Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning (MEL) for CEIF aims to maximise the efficiency, effectiveness, impact and sustainability of the umbrella CEIF platform. MEL also aims to strengthen the evidence base and address a key research gap on clean energy innovation for climate change mitigation in ODA eligible countries. The objectives for evaluation and learning are (1) to strengthen the monitoring approach, (2) perform independent evaluations of CEIF, (3) to facilitate learning and effective knowledge dissemination, (4) to assess the Value for Money and (5) to help inform and shape future decision making in the ICF climate innovation portfolio.</narrative>
  </description>
